if he will recognise me and notice me with his eyes,
or will fail to know me, who for a long time have been apart.”

Not in truth for idleness’ sake does your lord not care for you,
nor does anything slavish show itself, to look upon,
in your form and size;

A man once I entertained in my dear fatherland,
who came to our house, and not yet any other mortal
of friendly strangers from far-off lands has come to my house;

for if you had found him alive in the land of Ithaca,
then well with gifts, having requited you, he would have sent you off
and with good hospitality;

whom, I suppose, far from his dear ones and from his fatherland
either in the open-sea the fishes ate, or on dry land
to beasts and birds prey he became;

nor his wife, rich in gifts, sound-minded Penelope,
wailed on the bed for her own husband, as was fitting,
having closed his eyes;

And for Odysseus this is now the fifth year,
since he went from there and departed from my fatherland,
ill-fated one;

truly good were the birds for him as he went,
on the right, at which rejoicing I was sending him off,
and he rejoiced as he went;
